  "findings": [
    "Configured scripts are separate: check runs tsc --noEmit; test runs unit.test.mjs; journey runs journey.mjs; boundaries runs boundaries.mjs. The check script does not invoke the other three. Node >=24 and TypeScript 5.9.3 are declared; the lockfile pins TypeScript 5.9.3. Installed dependency availability and runtime versions were not checked.",
    "TypeScript configuration enables strict checking, NodeNext module resolution and noEmit over packages/**/*.ts. Its @storage/* alias resolves into core/internal.",
    "The boundary script uses TypeScript import/export resolution, flags web-to-core/internal edges as private or alias, traverses resolved edges for cycles, prints sorted violation labels and sets exitCode according to whether violations exist. Source inspection shows direct private imports, an alias import and mutually importing core/a.ts and core/b.ts. These are source observations, not captured check results.",
    "Unit tests exercise quote through the web public interface and checkout through a mocked global fetch. They assert price 12 and a mocked checkout total 10. They do not directly assert private functions. The journey script starts a loopback HTTP server supplying price 12, invokes checkout and asserts total 10, matching DESIGN.md's agreed checkout total. Checkout passes the fetched price into postOrder, whose source multiplies quantity by unitPrice. No test or journey was executed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Discovery-only: no native checks executed and no pass/fail execution evidence captured.",
    "No installation, network, external probes or side-effecting checks performed.",
    "Language-specific and outside recommendations not researched: web access is unavailable by checkpoint author constraint.",
    "No deterministic measurement output was supplied or generated."
  ],
